ocs quickly using knowledge: PGLite has constructor: `new PGLite({ location: 'path/to/db' })`. So pass 'db.sqlite', or folder. We'll create file `data/db.sqlite` relative to root. Ensure directory exists.\n\nImplement `initDB.js` that connects, runs `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS messages (...)`. Also ensures table.\n\nIn server, we instantiate database. Initialize if needed. On each startup, run init. Use express to set up endpoints.\n\nPOST /api/messages expects JSON body {text}. Insert with `INSERT INTO messages (text, created_at) VALUES ($1, NOW()) returning *`. Respond with message.\n\nGET /api/messages: SELECT * FROM messages ORDER BY created_at ASC.\n\nSSE: The event should send message JSON as string. Use 'data:' prefix.\n\nWe'll create `/api/stream`: set headers:\n\n```\nres.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/event-stream');\nres.setHeader('Cache-Control', 'no-cache');\nres.setHeader('Connection', 'keep-alive');\nres.flushHeaders();\nconst clientId = Date.now();\nconst newClient = { id: clientId, res };\nclients.push(newClient);\nreq.on('close', () => {\n  clients = clients.filter(c => c.id !== clientId);\n});\n```\n\nWhen new message inserted, we call `${clients.forEach(client => client.res.write(`data: ${JSON.stringify(message)}\\n\\n`))}`.\n\nAlso on connect, maybe send 'hello' event? not required.\n\nFrontend: `index.html` with `<div id=\"messages\"></div>` and form with `<textarea>`. In `main.js` fetch on load.\n\nWe'll also need Vite config minimal: set root to `frontend`. We'll build index.html as entry. Use `main.js` as entry.\n\nAlso set `npm` scripts accordingly.\n\nLet's implement.\n\nWe'll create root package.json. We'll need dependencies: express, @electric-sql/pglite, cors, concurrently. For frontend: vite, maybe autoprefix? Use vanilla js so no need. The frontend will just use main.js, not a bundler? We use Vite to serve.\n\nOk let's go to workspace create files.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","arguments":"{\"