ically to disk location if name is passed; Entities may be persisted to local file; It's okay.\n\n- We need to ensure server initialization creates table asynchronously before listening? Currently initDb called after server listens; but connection may attempt to read messages before table exists. But GET messages before table creation may error; but fine if request after startup. Minor.\n\n- Need to handle message insert returning \"RETURNING id, text, created_at\" - For pglite, use $1 placeholder? actual db.all expects query with placeholders? The all method in pglite is db.all(sql, ...params?). In our code, we passed 'text' variable directly; that's invalid. We'll adjust to use ? perhaps. Use db.all('INSERT INTO messages (text) VALUES ($1) RETURNING id, text, created_at', [text])? Let's check docs: The PGLite API may have async db.all(sql, ...params). So fine to pass text as array. We'll modify code accordingly.\n\nAlso the messages table creation query uses SERIAL; pglite supports that? Should.\n\nImplement modifications.\n\nLet's patch server/index.js accordingly.\n\nAlso modify front-end code.\n\nLet's write files:\n\nfrontend/index.html:\n\n```\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <title>Realtime Board</title>\n  <style>\n    body {font-family: sans-serif; padding: 1rem;}\n    #messages {list-style: none; padding:0;}\n    #messages li {margin-bottom: .5rem;}\n    form {margin-top: 1rem;}\n    input[type=text] {width: 80%; padding: .5rem;}\n    button {padding: .5rem 1rem;}\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h1>Realtime Board</h1>\n  <ul id=\"messages\"></ul>\n  <form id=\"message-form\">\n    <input type=\"text\" id=\"message-input\" placeholder=\"Type a message...\" required />\n    <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n  </form>\n  <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\nfrontend/src/main.js:\n\n```\nconst messagesEl = document.getElementById('messages');\nconst form = document.getElementById('message-form');\nconst input = document.getElementById('message-input');\n\nconst renderMessage = (msg) => {\n  const li = document.createElement('li');\n  li.textContent = `${new Date(msg.created_at).toLocaleTimeString()}: ${msg.text}`;\n  messagesEl.appendChild(li);\n};\n\nconst loadHistory = async () => {\n  const res = await fetch('/api/messages');\n  const msgs = await res.json();\n  msgs.forEach(renderMessage);\n};\n\nconst startSSE = () => {\n  const es = new EventSource('/api/stream');\n  es.addEventListener('message', e => {\n    const msg = JSON.parse(e.data);\n    renderMessage(msg);\n  });\n};\n\nform.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  const text = input.value.trim();\n  if (!text) return;\n  try {\n    await fetch('/api/messages', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},\n      body: JSON.stringify({text})\n    });\n    input.value = '';\n  } catch (err) { console.error(err); }\n});\n\n(async () => {\n  await loadHistory();\n  startSSE();\n})();\n```\n\nNow add frontend/vite.config.js:\n\n```\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite';\nexport default defineConfig({\n  root: '.',\n  build: {\n    outDir: '../dist'\n  },\n  server: {\n    proxy: {\n      '/api': 'http://localhost:5000'\n    }\n  }\n});\n```\n\nBut root directory of Vite is 'frontend', we may need to set root: '.' as inside frontend. The outDir maybe '../dist', but we likely want to build frontend dist. The root's default is 'frontend', but we can maintain default. To simplify, just leave defaults. We just need a proxy. So vite.config.js in frontend.\n\nAlso update server/index.js to correct query for insertion and to use async init before server listens maybe. Let's patch.\n\nAlso update root package.json to include dependencies.\n\nLet's patch accordingly.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","arguments":"{\"path\":\"package.json\",\"old_str\":\"\\\"scripts\\\": {\", \"new_str\":\"\\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"ex